# Encore Bridge settings (Windows)
#
# This file is %LOCALAPPDATA%\Encore\settings.env. Encore Bridge created it from a template the first
# time it ran, and never overwrites it: only the setup guide changes its SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID line. After
# you change something here, save the file, then choose Troubleshooting > Restart bridge in the Encore
# Bridge menu (the icon in the notification area). Close this file before you use the setup guide, so
# an older copy isn't saved over the guide's change.
#
# Format: one SETTING=value per line. Lines that start with # are notes and are ignored. Don't put
# quotes around values, and don't put a note on the same line as a value. An empty value means
# "use the default".
#
# Most people never need to change anything here: the setup guide on the admin page takes care of
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID, and everything else has a sensible default.


# The Client ID of YOUR OWN Spotify developer app. The setup guide (Encore Bridge menu > Setup guide...)
# fills this in for you, and the guide shows how to make the app. It is not a secret, but it is yours:
# don't use someone else's. If you change it here, connect your Spotify account again afterwards.
SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=


# The port the Encore app and the admin page use. 8095 unless another program already uses it.
# If you change it, also change the Home and Away addresses in the Encore app and the port forward
# on your router (setup guide step 8), and choose Troubleshooting > Fix firewall in the Encore
# Bridge menu so Windows Firewall lets the phone in.
PORT=8095


# The admin page password. Leave this empty: the admin page asks you to choose one the first time
# you open it on this PC (that is safer than keeping it in this file). A value here overrides the
# one chosen on the admin page.
#ADMIN_PASSWORD=


# Which addresses may open the admin page and pair a phone, as a comma-separated list of address
# ranges. The default allows home networks, this PC and VPN ranges. Only change it if you know
# you need to, for example to allow just your own home network:
#ADMIN_ALLOW=192.168.1.0/24


# Encore Bridge looks for a new version on GitHub once a day. It sends only its version number;
# GitHub sees this computer's public IP address, as with any download. Set this to 0 to turn the
# daily check off ("Check for updates" still works when you choose it).
#UPDATE_CHECK=1
